v = \sqrt{\frac{8 \times 8.314 \, \text{J/mol} \cdot \text{K} \times 298 \, \text{K}}{\pi \times 0.222 \, \text{kg/mol}}}
\]

First, calculate the numerator:

\[
8 \times 8.314 \times 298 = 19077.664 \, \text{J/mol}
\]

Next, calculate the denominator:

\[
\pi \times 0.222 = 0.6944 \, \text{kg/mol}
\]

Now, divide the numerator by the denominator:

\[
\frac{19077.664 \, \text{J/mol}}{0.6944 \, \text{kg/mol}} = 27487.23 \, \text{m}^2/\text{s}^2
\]

Finally, take the square root of the result:

\[
v = \sqrt{27487.23 \, \text{m}^2/\text{s}^2} \approx 165.77 \, \text{m/s}
\]

Therefore, the mean molecular speed \( v \) of Radon (Rn) at standard room temperature is approximately \( 165.77 \, \text{m/s} \).

**Final Answer:**
The mean molecular speed \( v \) of Radon (Rn) is approximately \( 165.77 \, \text{m/s} \) at a temperature of \( 298 \, \text{K} \).


    
