By constructing the Turing machine \( M' \) as described, we have shown that every language \( L \in \textbf{P}_{\text{bad-angel}} \) can be decided by a deterministic polynomial-time Turing machine with oracle access to \( S \). This completes the construction and demonstrates that \( \textbf{P}_{\text{bad-angel}} \subseteq \textbf{P} \).

